feat(skills): align with 2026-07-26 → 2026-08-09 common PR reviews

Mined every review comment, self-review, and bot finding across the
non-release PRs merged in oneprojectorg/common since the last pass (#11,
through 2026-07-26) and folded the durable, generalizable conventions
into the existing skills (no new skill this pass). Bumps devtools to
0.15.0.

Themes folded in:

- i18n-strings — accessibility-facing strings (aria-label, textValue,
  placeholder) are user-facing and need t() (#1654); hooks call
  useTranslations for their own toast copy, and translate every string
  in the same surface (#1674); a missing key renders raw with no ICU
  interpolation, which is invisible on an aria-label (#1683); delete
  orphaned keys from all seven dictionaries (#1682/#1684); no hardcoded
  list separator (#1689).
- op-ui-conventions — Tailwind v4 drops a bare number in a typed utility
  (duration-450 emits no CSS; use duration-[450ms]) (#1688); the
  no-arbitrary-values rule covers every utility, not just sizing
  (#1673/#1726); tailwind-merge silently discards conflicting classes
  (#1671); a child cannot un-dim an opacity-dimmed ancestor (#1675);
  a11y — aria-label replaces visible text (#1711), pointer-events-none
  is not disabled (#1670), inert items must not be keyboard-reachable
  (#1669), no affordance the component can't honor (#1659), a stateful
  control's label tracks its state (#1711), aria-sort on sortable
  headers (#1702); next/image uses fill + object-cover in a CSS-sized
  container and `?? undefined` for an absent URL (#1670).
- component-file-structure — never declare a component inside another's
  render body; it remounts and drops focus (#1702); a decorative
  suspense child needs its own error boundary or its failure takes down
  the whole panel (#1689); loading defaults must match the settled state
  (#1692) and skeleton bar counts must match real content (#1693);
  disable a control while its mutation is in flight (#1683), give a
  confirm-dialog toggle a pending value (#1696), and don't enable an
  action whose payload is still loading (#1725); apply a permission
  guard to every element it governs (#1695) and link an entity through
  one canonical route (#1567).
- service-layer-structure — re-assert every gate inside the writing
  statement's WHERE, and give the concurrent-failure path its own error
  message (#1703); log a warning when an "impossible" branch fires
  (#1677); named re-exports over `export *` when only one symbol should
  be public (#1676/#1680).
- api-endpoints — `.min(1)` on optional id-like inputs so '' can't
  collide with a NULL sentinel under a COALESCE unique index, applied to
  every sibling procedure (#1679/#1690); narrowing an output enum is a
  data-compatibility change (#1666).
- access-control — order OR'd grant checks so the broadest
  short-circuits before a lookup that can throw, and make an
  authorization path fail with UnauthorizedError rather than propagating
  a NotFoundError (#1694).
- drizzle-migrations — findFirst on a non-unique column needs a
  disambiguating filter (#1658).
- test-conventions — stable selectors over structural DOM traversal, and
  a comment must match its assertions (#1699); test helpers throw like
  production instead of no-opping (#1694).
- code-conventions — resolve, or explicitly defer with a reason, the
  debt a migration carries over (#1661/#1685/#1711).

Co-Authored-By: Scott Cazan <scottcazan@gmail.com>
